.TH CTI-VMSCAN 1 "2026-11-07" "cti-agent 1.6" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-vmscan \- combine the week's Qualys VM scan-result notices into one report
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti-vmscan
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR DURATION ]
.RB [ \-\-scans
.IR TITLES ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-text\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-subject\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-seen\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-coverage ]
.RB [ \-\-subnets\-file
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-csv\-out
.IR FILE ]
.PP
.B cti-vmscan \-\-commit\-seen
.I FILE
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-vmscan
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-vmscan
reads the
.B "Qualys: Scan Results"
notices that arrived in the CTI mailbox over the last week (Graph, read-only),
takes the newest result for each scheduled scan it is told to expect, and
renders one notice with the scans kept separate: that each ran, when and for
how long, how many addresses it scanned and how many were alive, and the
locations it covered (its Qualys Target Groups).
.PP
It carries no vulnerability counts or severities, on purpose. The report goes
to people who do not act on them from here, and the two scans overlap, so the
counts would confuse more than they tell. The notice parser still reads them;
the report does not show them.
.SS The coverage check
It also checks the network spreadsheet (the source of authority for what
networks exist) against the Qualys Asset Groups the scans cover, by ADDRESS, not
by name, because the scans' Target Group names and the spreadsheet's location
names do not match. For each active location it takes the networks that count as
its corporate network (the rows labelled
.BR corp ,
or whichever rows an operator rule names) and reports:
.TP
.B NOT SCANNED
A corp network in no Asset Group, in a group no weekly scan covers, or only partly
inside the scanned groups. This is how a missed location shows up. The lane
records only that it is not scanned: why differs from one location to the next
(not set up yet, not reachable, no network architecture yet) and the security team
cannot check which, so the network and M&A teams are asked to say. The worksheet
has a blank column for their answer.
.TP
.B FIX OR CLARIFY IN THE SPREADSHEET
A location the check could not use: a corp row with no network written in it, a
corp network that is not a valid CIDR, one outside the location's own block (a
likely typo), one that overlaps another location's, or no row that clearly counts
as the corp network. The location is not checked until this is fixed, or an
rule in FILES says which rows count. The lane never guesses, and the fix is the
network team's: the security team only reads the spreadsheet.
.TP
.B CHECK IN QUALYS
A scanned Asset Group whose addresses appear nowhere in the spreadsheet, a group
with no IP ranges (so it cannot be checked), or a Target Group the scan names
that Qualys has no Asset Group for.
.PP
Every line names the location, the spreadsheet row to look at, and what to do, so
the report can go to the network and acquisitions teams as well as security. The
email ends with a short note on how the spreadsheet has to be laid out to be read
(a header row per location, a row labelled corp with a CIDR, DECOMMISSIONED for
retired locations), and the same findings come as a worksheet
.RB ( \-\-csv\-out ,
attached by
.BR run\-vmscan ).
.PP
Decommissioned, free and open-to-use locations are skipped. If the check cannot
run (the spreadsheet or the Asset Groups cannot be read) the report says so; it
is never shown as a clean result. The check only reads: it changes nothing in
Qualys or in the spreadsheet.
.PP
It sends nothing. It is run by
.BR run\-vmscan (1),
which hands the files to
.BR cti\-mailer (1)
\-\-lane vmscan.
.PP
A scheduled scan that left no result in the window is the first thing the
report says, and its subject begins
.BR [NO\ RESULT] ;
a scan that did not finish is flagged
.BR [INCOMPLETE] .
.PP
A message with the results subject that did not come from Qualys is not read.
It is logged with a pointer to the usual cause, a schedule whose notification
From Address is set to this mailbox. Set it to qualys@qualys.net.
.PP
Only the results notices of the expected scans are recorded as used. The other
Qualys notices for the same scan (Scan Completed, the owner-only notification,
scan scheduled to start) carry nothing the report uses and are left alone.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-since " DURATION"
How far back to look for scan-result notices. Default 168h.
.TP
.BI \-\-scans " TITLES"
Comma-separated titles of the scheduled scans to combine. Default
.BR VMSCAN_SCANS ,
else
.B Weekly Scheduled Scan for non\-REDACTED-SUB/REDACTED-SUB
and
.BR "REDACTED-SUB/REDACTED-SUB Weekly" .
Titles are compared ignoring case and spacing.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Write the HTML report here (mode 0600).
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-out " FILE"
Write the plain-text version here.
.TP
.BI \-\-subject\-out " FILE"
Write the subject line here, so the runner need not run a second time.
.TP
.BI \-\-seen\-out " FILE"
Write the notices this report covered here, as JSON, for
.BR \-\-commit\-seen .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-coverage
Skip the coverage check.
.TP
.BI \-\-subnets\-file " FILE"
Read the network spreadsheet (an .xlsx) from this file instead of SharePoint,
for a manual test.
.TP
.BI \-\-csv\-out " FILE"
Write the coverage findings as a worksheet (CSV) here: category, location, sheet
row, network, asset group and what to do. Written only when there is something to
work through. Cells that would open as a formula are made inert.
.TP
.BI \-\-commit\-seen " FILE"
Record a
.B \-\-seen\-out
file in the VM scan lane's processed log, then exit. The mailbox cleanup reads
that log and archives those notices once they are 48 hours old.
.B run\-vmscan
does this only after a real send.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VMSCAN_SCANS
The scans to combine, by title, comma separated.
.TP
.B SUBNETS_DRIVE_ID
.TQ
.B SUBNETS_ITEM_ID
Where the network spreadsheet lives in SharePoint (the drive and the file). The
Graph app registration needs permission to read that file as an application:
.B Sites.Selected
with a read grant on the site, or
.BR Files.Read.All .
.TP
.B SUBNETS_SHEET
The worksheet to read. Default
.BR Sites .
.TP
.B NETRULES_FILE
Optional security-team rules for locations the spreadsheet does not make clear. Default
.IR /etc/cti\-agent/netrules.txt .
.TP
.B QUALYS_BASE_URL
.TQ
.B QUALYS_USERNAME
.TQ
.B QUALYS_PASSWORD
The Qualys API account, to list the Asset Groups (read-only).
.TP
.B FLEET_ORG
The organisation name in the report header.
.PP
The Graph settings are those of the other lanes
.RB ( TENANT_ID ,
.BR CLIENT_ID ,
.BR CLIENT_SECRET ,
.BR GRAPH_MAILBOX ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/netrules.txt
Optional, root-owned: the security team's own record about a location, one per line. The normal fix for a location the spreadsheet does not make clear is for the network team to correct the spreadsheet; this is only for what the security team decides to do meanwhile. A line is
.B location | use ROLE,ROLE
(these row labels count as its corp network) or
.B location | ignore
(leave it out of the check). The location is the start of its header in the
spreadsheet. Lines starting with # are comments.
.TP
.I $FLEET_HOME/state/processed\-vmscan.json
The notices this lane has used, written by
.BR \-\-commit\-seen .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was written. A missing or unfinished scan is in the report, not an
error.
.TP
.B 1
The mailbox could not be read, a file could not be written, or the processed
log does not parse.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render this week's report without sending it:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-vmscan \-\-out /tmp/vm.html \-\-text\-out /tmp/vm.txt
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-vmscan (1),
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR cti\-mailbox (1)
